=== get_markdown ===
Free and open source software for everybody. All instances are hosted and maintained by a non-profit 0011.LT. To help maintain long term availability of these instances please consider donating . For a better decentralization and reduced energy waste for sending zeros and ones accross the internet it is recommended to use these instances if you are located in Lithuania. Otherwise consider looking for other instances that would be hosted closer to you

Forgejo registration is temporarily disabled

##### Jitsi Meet

Jitsi Meet is used for video conferencing. In addition to audio and video, screen sharing is available. New members can be invited via a generated link

##### Mastodon

Mastodon is a software for running self-hosted social networking services. It has micro blogging features similar to „Twitter“ which are offered by a large number of independently run nodes, known as instances or servers, each with its own code of conduct, terms of service, privacy policy, privacy options, and content moderation policies

##### PeerTube

PeerTube is a decentralized, ActivityPub federated video platform powered by WebTorrent, that uses peer-to-peer technology to reduce load on individual servers when viewing videos

##### SearXNG

SearXNG is a free and open-source federated metasearch engine. It is hosted by several instances, public and private

##### CryptPad

CryptPad is a collaboration suite that is end-to-end encrypted and open-source. It is designed to facilitate collaboration by synchronizing changes to documents in real time

##### Element

Element is a free and open-source software instant messaging client implementing the Matrix protocol. Home server address is matrix.0011.lt

##### Forgejo

Forgejo is open source software for hosting code using the Git version control system to aid with software development

